"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkplacepilot_frontend||=[]).push([[556],{8556(e,n,t){t.r(n),t.d(n,{default:()=>s});t(5043);var i=t(5475),a=t(579);function s(){return(0,a.jsxs)("div",{style:{fontFamily:"Inter, sans-serif",background:"#f8fafc",minHeight:"100vh"},children:[(0,a.jsxs)("nav",{style:{background:"#1e1b4b",padding:"16px 40px",display:"flex",alignItems:"center",justifyContent:"space-between"},children:[(0,a.jsxs)("div",{style:{display:"flex",alignItems:"center",gap:10},children:[(0,a.jsx)("div",{style:{width:36,height:36,background:"linear-gradient(135deg,#818cf8,#4f46e5)",borderRadius:10,display:"flex",alignItems:"center",justifyContent:"center",fontWeight:800,color:"white",fontSize:13},children:"PP"}),(0,a.jsx)("span",{style:{fontSize:18,fontWeight:800,color:"white"},children:"PlacePilot"})]}),(0,a.jsx)(i.N_,{to:"/",style:{color:"rgba(255,255,255,0.7)",fontSize:13},children:"\u2190 Back to Home"})]}),(0,a.jsxs)("div",{style:{maxWidth:900,margin:"0 auto",padding:"60px 24px"},children:[(0,a.jsx)("h1",{style:{fontSize:38,fontWeight:800,marginBottom:12,color:"#1e293b"},children:"Project Methodology"}),(0,a.jsx)("p",{style:{color:"#64748b",fontSize:16,marginBottom:48},children:"PlacePilot \u2014 Adaptive Explainable Placement Readiness Engine"}),[{n:"01",title:"Problem Statement",body:'Students preparing for placements use 5\u20137 different platforms: HackerRank for coding, IndiaBix for aptitude, LinkedIn for resume, Pramp for interviews, and LeetCode for DSA. Their performance is scattered across all these tools, making it impossible to answer: "Am I ready for this specific job role \u2014 and why?"\n\nPlacement officers face the same challenge: they cannot easily identify which students need help, which skills are batch-wide weaknesses, or which student is closest to being placement-ready.'},{n:"02",title:"Research Gap",body:"Existing platforms either focus on one domain (coding, aptitude, or resume) or provide generic recommendations that do not account for the student's individual performance. No existing platform integrates multiple data sources, applies explainable ML to predict readiness, and maps the prediction to specific job role requirements simultaneously."},{n:"03",title:"Proposed Solution",body:"PlacePilot is an integrated platform that:\n\u2022 Collects student data across 7+ performance dimensions\n\u2022 Builds a unified skill profile per student  \n\u2022 Compares the profile against target job role requirements\n\u2022 Predicts placement readiness using Random Forest (not GenAI)\n\u2022 Explains the prediction using SHAP values\n\u2022 Generates a personalised action plan using Gemini GenAI\n\u2022 Updates readiness whenever new assessment data is added"},{n:"04",title:"Core Innovation",body:'The "Adaptive Explainable Placement Readiness Engine" is the key innovation.\n\nUnlike traditional approaches that use a single score or generic checklist, this engine:\n1. Accepts 12 performance features from multiple sources\n2. Runs Random Forest classification (Ready / Moderately Ready / Needs Improvement)\n3. Computes SHAP values to explain each prediction in plain language\n4. Calculates role-specific skill gaps by comparing against RoleRequirements\n5. Ranks gaps by priority (gap \xd7 weight)\n6. Sends the gap analysis to Gemini for a personalized weekly plan\n7. Stores all results and updates on every new assessment\n\nThe same student will have DIFFERENT readiness levels for different roles because each role has different skill weights.'},{n:"05",title:"Algorithm Details",body:'Random Forest:\n\u2022 Trained on 800 synthetic samples (clearly labelled as demo data)\n\u2022 12 features: academic, DSA, programming, DBMS, OOP, aptitude, coding test, technical test, interview, resume, LeetCode, communication\n\u2022 100 estimators, max_depth=10, balanced class weights\n\u2022 Demo accuracy: ~85% on synthetic test set\n\u2022 Code structured so a real institutional dataset can replace synthetic data immediately\n\nSHAP:\n\u2022 TreeExplainer on the trained Random Forest\n\u2022 Returns per-feature contribution values\n\u2022 Positive SHAP = contributed toward "Ready"\n\u2022 Negative SHAP = contributed toward lower readiness\n\u2022 Falls back to rule-based approximation if shap library unavailable\n\nGenAI (Gemini):\n\u2022 Receives student name, actual skill scores, top gaps, and role name\n\u2022 Generates: summary, 4-week plan, skill actions, resources, next steps\n\u2022 Falls back to deterministic data-driven recommendations if API key not provided\n\u2022 All recommendations clearly labelled as demo when no real Gemini key'},{n:"06",title:"System Architecture",body:"Frontend:  React 18 + React Router + Recharts + Axios\nBackend:   FastAPI (Python 3.11) + SQLAlchemy ORM\nDatabase:  PostgreSQL 15\nML Layer:  scikit-learn Random Forest + SHAP\nGenAI:     Google Gemini Pro API (demo fallback included)\nAuth:      JWT Bearer tokens + bcrypt password hashing\nDeployment: Docker Compose (db + backend + frontend)\n\nData Flow:\nStudent takes test \u2192 Score stored \u2192 Skill profile recalculated \u2192\nRandom Forest predicts readiness \u2192 SHAP explains prediction \u2192\nSkill gaps identified \u2192 GenAI generates action plan \u2192\nDashboard updated \u2192 History recorded"},{n:"07",title:"Limitations & Disclaimers",body:"\u2022 The ML model is trained on SYNTHETIC data. It is a proof-of-concept demonstrating the pipeline.\n\u2022 Readiness scores are NOT a guarantee of placement success.\n\u2022 The model needs real historical placement outcome data from your institution for production use.\n\u2022 LeetCode data is manually entered (no live API due to access restrictions).\n\u2022 Resume analysis uses keyword matching, not NLP parsing.\n\u2022 SHAP values on synthetic data should be interpreted as directional indicators, not absolute truths.\n\u2022 GenAI recommendations use a demo engine when no Gemini API key is configured."},{n:"08",title:"Future Scope",body:"\u2022 GitHub integration \u2014 auto-pull contribution stats\n\u2022 LinkedIn integration \u2014 experience and skills sync\n\u2022 Company-specific mock interviews\n\u2022 Recruiter dashboard\n\u2022 Mobile app (React Native)\n\u2022 Multi-college support with college admin role\n\u2022 Real NLP-based resume parsing\n\u2022 Live LeetCode API integration\n\u2022 Ensemble model with XGBoost and neural network\n\u2022 Continuous model retraining as placement outcomes are recorded"}].map(e=>(0,a.jsxs)("div",{style:{marginBottom:40,display:"flex",gap:24},children:[(0,a.jsx)("div",{style:{fontSize:28,fontWeight:800,color:"#e2e8f0",flexShrink:0,width:40},children:e.n}),(0,a.jsxs)("div",{children:[(0,a.jsx)("h2",{style:{fontSize:20,fontWeight:700,marginBottom:12,color:"#1e293b"},children:e.title}),(0,a.jsx)("div",{style:{background:"white",borderRadius:12,padding:24,border:"1px solid #e2e8f0",fontSize:14,color:"#475569",lineHeight:1.9,whiteSpace:"pre-line"},children:e.body})]})]},e.n)),(0,a.jsxs)("div",{style:{background:"#1e1b4b",color:"white",borderRadius:16,padding:32,textAlign:"center",marginTop:40},children:[(0,a.jsx)("h3",{style:{fontSize:20,fontWeight:700,marginBottom:12},children:"PlacePilot Research Statement"}),(0,a.jsx)("p",{style:{color:"rgba(255,255,255,0.6)",fontSize:14,maxWidth:600,margin:"0 auto",lineHeight:1.8},children:'"PlacePilot transforms scattered placement preparation data into a role-specific, explainable, and continuously updated student readiness profile \u2014 bridging the gap between student effort and employer expectations."'}),(0,a.jsx)("div",{style:{marginTop:24},children:(0,a.jsx)(i.N_,{to:"/register",style:{display:"inline-block",padding:"12px 32px",background:"#4f46e5",color:"white",borderRadius:8,fontWeight:700,fontSize:14},children:"Try the Platform"})})]})]})]})}}}]);
